WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.335
[g@Sun Wukong put his hand on the iron pillar.

2
00:00:08.336 --> 00:00:10.501
He felt it move.@g]

3
00:00:10.502 --> 00:00:15.419
"Hmm," he thought. "This piece of iron really is magical.

4
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.457
I bet it will do whatever I want it to do."

5
00:00:18.458 --> 00:00:21.376
"Smaller!" commanded Wukong.

6
00:00:21.377 --> 00:00:23.287
[g@The pillar shrank!

7
00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:29.162
Soon it was just a little taller than Wukong.@g]

8
00:00:29.163 --> 00:00:33.778
He picked it up and swung it around.

9
00:00:33.779 --> 00:00:38.117
"This is a perfect weapon for me," he said.

10
00:00:38.118 --> 00:00:42.503
"I can't believe he can lift it!" said the Dragon Queen.

11
00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:45.859
Wukong made the bar even smaller.

12
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:48.980
[g@Soon it was no bigger than a pin.

13
00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:54.379
He placed it inside his ear.@g]

14
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.626
"I've got what I want," said Wukong. "Good-bye."

15
00:00:58.627 --> 00:01:03.611
He turned around and left.

16
00:01:03.612 --> 00:01:07.768
"He was very rude," said the Dragon Queen.

17
00:01:07.769 --> 00:01:10.853
The Dragon King clenched his fists.

18
00:01:10.854 --> 00:01:18.273
"I'm going to report him to the Jade Emperor!"

19
00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:24.038
Back home, the others were amazed by Wukong's new weapon.

20
00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:28.751
"Nobody will ever attack us again!" declared Wukong.

21
00:01:28.752 --> 00:01:31.456
The monkeys and apes cheered.

22
00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:39.371
They held a big feast that lasted until late at night.

23
00:01:39.372 --> 00:01:44.521
[g@Wukong went to bed happy.

24
00:01:44.522 --> 00:01:49.521
But as he fell asleep, two spirits grabbed him.@g]

25
00:01:49.522 --> 00:01:52.277
[g@"What are you doing?" asked Wukong.

26
00:01:52.278 --> 00:02:00.208
"Let go of me!"@g]

27
00:02:00.209 --> 00:02:05.849
He kicked and struggled as the spirits dragged him out of his cave.

28
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.950
They walked toward a dark and creepy city.

29
00:02:08.951 --> 00:02:14.607
A sign on the entrance gate said "Land of Darkness."

30
00:02:14.608 --> 00:02:17.972
"The Land of Darkness?" cried Wukong.

31
00:02:17.973 --> 00:02:20.750
[g@"That's where people go when they die.

32
00:02:20.751 --> 00:02:25.538
I'm supposed to live forever!"@g]

33
00:02:25.539 --> 00:02:28.243
[g@He yanked his arms free.

34
00:02:28.244 --> 00:02:30.636
"Grow!" he cried.@g]

35
00:02:30.637 --> 00:02:34.181
[g@His iron bar quickly grew.

36
00:02:34.182 --> 00:02:39.036
[i@Whap!@i] He knocked out the first spirit.@g]

37
00:02:39.037 --> 00:02:43.946
[i@Crack!@i] He knocked out the second spirit.

38
00:02:43.947 --> 00:02:49.129
Wukong stomped into the Land of Darkness.

39
00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:54.081
He headed toward the Palace of Darkness.

40
00:02:54.082 --> 00:02:58.755
[g@As he went, he swung his iron bar back and forth.

41
00:02:58.756 --> 00:03:02.497
Demons and ghosts fled.@g]

42
00:03:02.498 --> 00:03:06.742
A tall spirit stepped out of the palace.

43
00:03:06.743 --> 00:03:10.412
"What's going on out here?" the spirit asked.

44
00:03:10.413 --> 00:03:13.183
"Who are you?" asked Wukong.

45
00:03:13.184 --> 00:03:17.138
"I am the Judge of the Dead," said the spirit.

46
00:03:17.139 --> 00:03:20.584
"Why are you causing all this trouble?"

47
00:03:20.585 --> 00:03:24.247
[g@"I want to know why I was brought here," said Wukong.

48
00:03:24.248 --> 00:03:26.177
"Tell me now!"@g]

49
00:03:26.178 --> 00:03:28.736
The judge held up his hands.

50
00:03:28.737 --> 00:03:33.814
"If you were brought here, it means your time on Earth is over."

51
00:03:33.815 --> 00:03:38.919
"Nonsense!" yelled Wukong. "I'm going to live forever!"

52
00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.283
[g@The judge looked nervous.

53
00:03:41.284 --> 00:03:44.225
"Let's check the Directory," he said.@g]

54
00:03:44.226 --> 00:03:49.476
"The Directory contains the name and age of every creature on Earth.

55
00:03:49.477 --> 00:03:54.050
It says when each creature will die."

56
00:03:54.051 --> 00:03:58.615
Inside the palace the judge opened a large book.

57
00:03:58.616 --> 00:04:01.577
"What is your name?" he asked.

58
00:04:01.578 --> 00:04:03.612
[g@Wukong told him.

59
00:04:03.613 --> 00:04:06.247
The judge flipped through the pages.@g]

60
00:04:06.248 --> 00:04:08.637
[g@"Here it is," said the judge.

61
00:04:08.638 --> 00:04:11.510
"It says 'Sun Wukong.@g]

62
00:04:11.511 --> 00:04:18.199
Born from a stone three hundred years ago. Died today.'"

63
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.218
[g@Wukong shook his head.

64
00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:23.432
"No. I'm going to live forever."@g]

65
00:04:23.433 --> 00:04:26.683
"The Directory isn't wrong," said the judge.

66
00:04:26.684 --> 00:04:31.994
"You'll have to stay here now."

67
00:04:31.995 --> 00:04:36.343
[g@Wukong raised his iron bar and glared at the judge.

68
00:04:36.344 --> 00:04:38.971
"Give me that book!"@g]

69
00:04:38.972 --> 00:04:40.720
[g@The judge hesitated.

70
00:04:40.721 --> 00:04:42.760
"I can't give it to—"@g]

71
00:04:42.761 --> 00:04:45.512
"Now!" said Wukong.

72
00:04:45.513 --> 00:04:51.430
Shaking, the judge handed the book to Wukong.

73
00:04:51.431 --> 00:04:55.042
Wukong plucked two of his hairs and blew on them.

74
00:04:55.043 --> 00:04:59.295
[g@They turned into a brush and a jar of ink.

75
00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:02.794
He drew a line through his name.@g]

76
00:05:02.795 --> 00:05:06.211
"You can't do that!" said the judge.

77
00:05:06.212 --> 00:05:09.462
"Yes, I can," said Wukong.

78
00:05:09.463 --> 00:05:16.974
Next, Wukong found the names of all the other monkeys and apes.

79
00:05:16.975 --> 00:05:22.810
He crossed out their names too.

80
00:05:22.811 --> 00:05:26.933
"Now I really will live forever," said Wukong.

81
00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:33.059
"And so will all of my subjects!"

